Usage: dspace [command-name] {parameters}

Commands from launcher.xml
 - anonymize-statistics: Anonymize the ip values of the solr statistics
 - bitstore-migrate: Assetstore migration tool
 - checker: Run the checksum checker
 - checker-emailer: Send emails related to the checksum checker
 - classpath: Calculate and display the DSpace classpath
 - cleanup: Remove deleted bitstreams from the assetstore
 - community-filiator: Tool to manage community and sub-community relationships
 - create-administrator: Create a DSpace administrator account
 - database: Perform database tasks like test database connection, migrate/repair database, remove database
 - doi-organiser: Run the DOI organiser
 - dsprop: View a DSpace property from dspace.cfg
 - dsrun: Run a class directly
 - embargo-lifter: Embargo manager tool used to check, list and lift embargoes
 - generate-sitemaps: Generate search engine and html sitemaps
 - harvest: Manage the OAI-PMH harvesting of external collections
 - healthcheck: Create health check report
 - iiif-canvas-dimensions: Automatically add the IIIF canvas width/height metadata to Bitstreams of IIIF enabled Items.
 - index-authority: Indexes all metadata fields that use solr authority
 - index-deduplication: Update Deduplication Solr Search Index
 - initialize-entities: Initialize the entities with a provided xml
 - initialize-only-entity-types: Initialize only the entity types as needed by DSpace-CRIS
 - itemupdate: Item update tool for altering metadata and bitstream content in items
 - make-handle-config: Run the handle server simple setup command
 - migrate-embargo: Embargo manager tool used to migrate old version of Embargo to the new one included in dspace3
 - oai: OAI script manager
 - packager: Execute a packager
 - rdfizer: The RDFizer manages the attached triple store if dspace-rdf is enabled
 - read: Execute a stream of 'dspace' commands from a file or pipe
 - registry-loader: Load entries into a registry
 - retry-tracker: Retry all failed commits to the OpenURLTracker
 - solr-export-statistics: Export usage statistics data from Solr for back-up purposes
 - solr-import-statistics: Import usage statistics data (as previously exported using solr-export-statistics) into Solr
 - solr-reindex-statistics: Reindex the Solr-based usage statistics, for example after an upgrade that changes the schema
 - solr-upgrade-statistics-6x: Upgrade statistics (integer to UUID) to DSpace 6.x (or above) compatibility
 - stat-general: Compile the general statistics
 - stat-initial: Compile the initial statistics
 - stat-monthly: Compile the monthly statistics
 - stat-report-general: Create the general statistics report
 - stat-report-initial: Create the initial statistics report
 - stat-report-monthly: Create the monthly statistics report
 - stats-log-converter: Convert dspace.log files ready for import into solr statistics
 - stats-log-importer: Import previously converted log files into solr statistics
 - stats-util: Statistics Client for Maintenance of Solr Statistics Indexes
 - structure-builder: Build DSpace community and collection structure
 - test-email: Test the DSpace email server settings are OK
 - update-handle-prefix: Update handle records and metadata when moving from one handle to another
 - user: Manipulate a normal user account
 - validate-date: interactively validate date values against the multi-format date parser (good for testing custom regular expression configurations)
 - version: Display the version of DSpace and other troubleshooting information

Commands from script service
 - bulk-access-control: Bulk access control
 - bulk-import: Perform the bulk import of an excel file with a list of item to add, update or remove
 - bulk-item-export: Perform the multiple items export in the given format
 - collection-export: Perform the export of all the archived items of the given collection in xls format
 - cris-layout-tool: Script to import CRIS layout configuration from excel file
 - curate: Curation tasks
 - export: Batch Export to Simple Archive Format (SAF)
 - export-cris-layout-tool: Script to export CRIS layout configuration into excel file
 - export-schema: Exports a given schema into target registry file specified
 - filter-media: Perform the media filtering to extract full text from documents and to create thumbnails
 - harvest: Manage the OAI-PMH harvesting of external collections
 - import: Batch Import from Simple Archive Format (SAF)
 - import-openaire-events: Import new Openaire quality assurance broker events
 - import-openaire-suggestions: Imports suggestions from OpenAIRE for publication claim
 - import-publications: Perform the creating of workspace item using external sources (i.e. Scopus, WebOfScience)
 - index-discovery: Update Discovery Solr Search Index
 - item-enhancer: Script that allows to enhance all items
 - item-export: Perform the item export in the given format
 - metadata-deletion: Delete all the values of the specified metadata field
 - metadata-export: Export metadata for batch editing
 - metadata-export-search: export metadata from a discovery search
 - metadata-import: Import metadata after batch editing
 - orcid-bulk-pull: Perform a bulk pull from the ORCID registry for all the profiles with an ORCID id set
 - orcid-bulk-push: Perform the bulk synchronization of all the BATCH configured ORCID entities placed in the ORCID queue
 - process-cleaner: Cleanup all the old processes in the specified state
 - retry-tracker: Retry all failed commits to the OpenURLTracker
 - solr-database-resync: Update the database status of Items in solr
 - store-metrics: Perform the metrics storage
 - submission-forms-migrate: Script for migrating submission forms to DSpace 7
 - subscription-send: Send emails related to Community/Collection/Item subscriptions
 - update-item-references: Perform the resolution of authority references
 - update-metrics: Perform the metrics update using external source, taking first items that have been updated less recently
 - update-metrics-in-solr: Perform the metrics update in SOLR documents
